            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DEE C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was actually better than I expected. I used it with asparagus. The combo of tastes worked but it needed something sharp to balance the richness of the sesame oil/mayo. Not extra lemon, though. Maybe a tiny splash of rice wine vinegar? I sprinkled some Hawaiian black sea salt on top of the dip &amp; that helped add crunch &amp; an interesting flavor. Pretty cool recipe with few ingredients, proving that something doesn't need to be complicated to taste good. Thanks:o)"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
